                "retweet_count": 20,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "The COVID-19 pandemic uncovered a critical vulnerability in our healthcare system: our overreliance on foreign nations for essential medications.\n\nToday, 80% of active pharmaceutical ingredients are produced overseas. China and India together account for 85% of filings \u2014 and they also receive the highest number of FDA warning letters for serious violations, like carcinogens in medicines, destroying or falsifying data, and non-sterile manufacturing. \n\nFor both the health & safety of Floridians and the stability of our drug supply, we are examining ways to address these issues, and I thank Chairman Scott for leading this important hearing.",
